IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tfm-dates`
IMPORT `tfm-rules`

-- Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas) -- the questions of the BENEFICIARY of the estate who answers a claim.
--
-- SEAT: a person who takes under the will or the intestacy, and whose share bears the provision the Court orders for a
-- claimant: "Must I be served with the summons?", "Can I apply to have the order changed?", "How much of the provision
-- falls on my share?", "Can what I have already been given be taken back?". The claimant's seat is tfm-seat.l4; the two
-- draw on the same rules in tfm-rules.l4 and keep their own names. The executor or administrator (who acts for the
-- estate), the Court and the judge get no seat.
--
