-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas): the beneficiary's questions`

§§ `The claim`
-- Arises only once someone has claimed provision out of the estate.

@export Must a claimant's summons for provision out of the estate be served on me (Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas) s 4(2))? Yes if you are the executor of the will, the person granted letters of administration with the will annexed, or the administrator of an intestate estate, or if the Court or a judge has directed that you be served. The Act does not require service on other beneficiaries unless the Court so directs.
GIVEN `am I the executor or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the executor of the will, the person granted letters of administration with the will annexed, or the administrator of the intestate estate
      `has the Court directed that I be served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court or a judge has directed that the summons be served on you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the claimant's summons be served on me` MEANS
    `s 4(2) -- the summons must be served on me` `am I the executor or administrator` `has the Court directed that I be served`

@export How much of the provision ordered for a claimant falls on my part of the estate (Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas) s 10A)? Unless the Court orders otherwise, a payment ordered falls ratably on the whole estate (or on the part within the Court's authority): your part bears the payment times your part's value divided by the value of that estate. Nothing falls on a part the Court has exonerated or a part outside its authority. If the Court has ordered otherwise, its order decides.
GIVEN `the payment ordered` IS A NUMBER @desc The payment the order directs to be made for the claimant, in dollars
      `the value of my part of the estate` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of your part of the estate, in dollars
      `the value of the estate within the Court's authority` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the whole estate, or of the part of it subject to the Court's authority if its authority does not extend to the whole, in dollars
      `is my part within the Court's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your part of the estate is subject to the authority of the Court (for example, not property outside Tasmania beyond its reach)
      `has the Court exonerated my part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has exonerated your part of the estate from the incidence of the order (s 10A(2), (3))
      `has the Court ordered the incidence otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered that the payment fall otherwise than ratably on the estate
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of the provision falls on my part of the estate` MEANS
    `s 10A -- the part of the payment falling on my part of the estate` `the payment ordered` `the value of my part of the estate` `the value of the estate within the Court's authority` `is my part within the Court's authority` `has the Court exonerated my part` `has the Court ordered the incidence otherwise`

@export Can what has already been distributed to me from the estate be disturbed by a claim or by a change to an order (Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas) ss 9(5A), 11(4))? No, if it was distributed before the claimant applied for an extension of time (for a claim out of time), or if it was lawfully distributed before an application to alter an order. For a claim taken out in time, and in other cases, the Act does not say.
GIVEN `what application is it` IS A `The application` @desc The application: a claim taken out within the time; a claim needing an extension of time; or an application to alter an order
      `was it distributed to me before that application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the part of the estate was distributed to you before the application was made (for a claim out of time, before the application for an extension of time)
      `was the distribution lawfully made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the distribution to you was lawfully made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can what was distributed to me be disturbed` MEANS
    `ss 11(4), 9(5A) -- the distribution to me may be disturbed` `what application is it` `was it distributed to me before that application` `was the distribution lawfully made`

§§ `After an order`
-- Arises only once the Court has made an order providing for a claimant.

@export Can I apply to the Court to rescind or alter an order that made provision for a claimant out of the estate (Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas) s 9(5), (6))? Yes if you are the executor or administrator, or beneficially entitled to or interested in any part of the estate; the Court may rescind the order or alter it at any time. You must then have notice of your application served on everyone who takes a benefit under the order, and an alteration cannot disturb a distribution lawfully made before you applied.
GIVEN `am I the executor or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the executor or administrator of the estate
      `am I beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are beneficially entitled to, or interested in, any part of the estate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply to rescind or alter the order` MEANS
    `s 9(5) -- I may apply to rescind or alter the order` `am I the executor or administrator` `am I beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate`
